- ISO 704 — Terminology work: Principles and methods
    - Delimiting vs incidental attributes. Alpha treats all attributes alike. Marking which ones actually distinguish a concept from its siblings gives the "Concept vs Example" test a real basis, and makes the design rule "remove attributes that do not serve the model" checkable rather than aesthetic.
    - Named dimensions. Your Map node (... explanation) is already the right syntactic slot. Write ... dimension: legal form above a subdivision, and any sibling set with two unlabelled dimensions becomes a lintable error. Your occupation status is the case in point — Employed, Self Employed, Unemployed, Retired is one dimension, but Contributor, Manager, Executive, Non Executive, Independent nested under Employed is a seniority dimension crossed with a governance dimension.
